{"reference":"Daniel 9","book":"Daniel","chapter":9,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"cultural_context","title":"A communal confession","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Daniel’s prayer speaks in the collective voice—“we have sinned”—as he confesses alongside his people. This communal confession should not be weaponized to blame persecuted Jewish people for state violence or to demand public confession from people who have survived abuse.","verse_refs":["Daniel 9:3-19"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_daniel_009_26b1bb82c9e839fb56a9ba38"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"inference"}]},{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Seventy years and seventy weeks","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"Daniel begins with Jeremiah’s promise concerning seventy years, then the vision answers with “seventy weeks.” The chapter thus rereads Jeremiah’s period of desolation and restoration in an expanded scheme. Readers have not agreed on the scheme’s starting point, its divisions, the identity of its anointed figures, its calendars, or its endpoint; it therefore does not authorize a certain modern date for the end. The “abomination” of verse 27 has a horizon in an Antiochene temple desecration, but later Jewish and Christian reuses of the image need to be identified rather than treated as one interpretation. Christian christological readings are later canonical and confessional readings and should not erase Daniel’s Jewish setting, readers, or continuing Jewish interpretation.","verse_refs":["Daniel 9:1-27","Daniel 9:20-27","Daniel 9:27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_daniel_009_9b3587ae1e3bd92ed3973b22"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_3","text":"Jeremiah 25 and 29 associate Babylonian domination and restoration with seventy years. Daniel belongs to a longer history of rereading that language, alongside later Jewish textual and liturgical reception and later Christian quotation, allusion, and christological interpretation. These varied forms of reuse should not simply be collapsed into direct prediction.","verse_refs":["Daniel 9:1-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_daniel_009_96e2bad81be89efab13605b3"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}